nt":{"ref":"Package_QFP:TQFP-100_14x14mm_P0.5mm","url":"https://gitlab.com/api/v4/projects/kicad%2Flibraries%2Fkicad-footprints/repository/files/Package_QFP.pretty%2FTQFP-100_14x14mm_P0.5mm.kicad_mod/raw?ref=a0dcd398e7ea4b00cdeb91efc35f09cceaa9097d"},"generatedFootprint":"TQFP-100_14x14mm_P0.5mm","pinout":false},"buy":[{"store":"LCSC","url":"https://www.lcsc.com/product-detail/C5613473.html","priceUsd":7.2},{"store":"DigiKey","url":"https://www.digikey.com/en/products/result?keywords=CY8C6245AZI-S3D72"},{"store":"Mouser","url":"https://www.mouser.com/c/?q=CY8C6245AZI-S3D72"},{"store":"JLCPCB parts","url":"https://jlcpcb.com/parts/componentSearch?searchTxt=C5613473"},{"store":"Octopart","url":"https://octopart.com/search?q=CY8C6245AZI-S3D72"}]}],"released":2017,"status":"active","datasheetUrl":"https://www.infineon.com/dgdl/Infineon-PSOC_6_MCU_CY8C62X8_CY8C62XA-DataSheet-v18_00-EN.pdf?fileId=8ac78c8c7d0d8da4017d0ee7d03a70b1","productUrl":"https://www.infineon.com/part/CY8C624ABZI-S2D44","notes":["No radio. PSoC 63 is the BLE line, and Infineon's Wi-Fi/BT kits pair a PSoC 62 with an external CYW43xxx combo chip.","Serial ports come from SCBs that are each UART, SPI or I2C at runtime, so the uart/i2c/spi counts are per-type maxima, not additive. CY8C62x8/xA has 13 SCBs: 8 UART/SPI/I2C, 4 UART/I2C only, and 1 Deep Sleep SPI/I2C. CY8C62x7 has 9 SCBs (8 + 1 Deep Sleep) and CY8C62x5 has 7 (6 + 1 Deep Sleep).","Peripherals differ by sub-line. CAN FD (1 block) exists only on CY8C62x5 (-S3D6x/-S3D7x parts). SD host: 2 on CY8C62x8/xA, 1 on 62x5, none on 62x7. I2S: 2 on 62x8/xA, 1 on 62x7, none on 62x5. The 12-bit DAC, 2 opamps and 12 UDBs are only on CY8C62x7.","USB is full-speed device/host only, with no high-speed PHY.","UDBs (62x7 only) and Smart I/O give some programmable logic, but they are not comparable to RP2040 PIO.","There is no ROM UART/USB bootloader, so blank chips must be flashed over SWD (KitProg3, MiniProg4 or J-Link). DFU/MCUboot can be added in firmware.","The Infineon Arduino core (arduino-core-psoc6) only supports the CY8CKIT-062S2-AI board (CY8C624ABZI-S2D44). Infineon's MicroPython port for PSoC 6 lives in Infineon's fork, not upstream MicroPython.","activeUaPerMhz is the CM4 at 1.1 V core (LP mode, needed for 150 MHz). The 0.9 V ULP mode (up to 50 MHz) gives 22-27 uA/MHz.","CapSense works on any GPIO except the dedicated CMOD capacitor pin, so touchChannels is the GPIO count minus one.","SMIF supports single, dual and quad SPI (octal and dual-quad on 62x7/62x8/62xA) with XIP and on-the-fly AES. externalFlashMaxMB assumes the 128 MB XIP window."],"sources":["https://www.infineon.com/dgdl/Infineon-PSOC_6_MCU_CY8C62X8_CY8C62XA-DataSheet-v18_00-EN.pdf?fileId=8ac78c8c7d0d8da4017d0ee7d03a70b1","https://www.infineon.com/dgdl/Infineon-PSOC_6_MCU_CY8C62x6_CY8C62x7-DataSheet-v14_00-EN.pdf?fileId=8ac78c8c7d0d8da4017d0ee4c9386bff","https://www.infineon.com/dgdl/Infineon-PSOC_6_MCU_CY8C62X5-DataSheet-v10_00-EN.pdf?fileId=8ac78c8c7d0d8da4017d0ee8cb86719c","https://www.infineon.com/part/CY8C624ABZI-S2D44","https://jlcpcb.com/partdetail/Infineon-CY8C624ABZIS2D44/C5370259","https://www.lcsc.com/product-detail/C2949340.html","https://www.digikey.com/en/products/detail/infineon-technologies/CY8C624AAZI-S2D44/16516837","https://www.digikey.com/en/products/detail/infineon-technologies/CY8C6245AZI-S3D72/16516838","https://github.com/Infineon/arduino-core-psoc6","https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/tree/main/boards/infineon/cy8ckit_062s2_ai"],"boards":[]}